# Self-similar tiled pattern completion

Goal: execute all four official labels, author fresh canonical completion and an opt-in post-completion cavity fill.

Design: recover regular separator bands and majority normal tile; the other repeated tile has a unique novel color whose micro-mask defines a macro template. Infer its unique translation covering the observed special tiles, then complete missing copies. The alternate floods the macro complement only after completion and fills enclosed cells. A wrong-order counterfactual floods the partial layout first.

Tasks:
- [x] Red original-label, count, privacy, geometry and topology tests.
- [x] Python engine and Racket canonical/alternate; native and ordinary resource-closed samplers.
- [x] Named-rival audit and fixed regressions; protected preflight, public isolation and causal replay.

Review focus: separator thickness; novel color including zero; ambiguous translations; diagonal leaks in cavity topology; distinct queries and setting-independent inputs; malformed cells.

Only this task home may change. No registration or approval. Author self-review, with exact-source replay and bounded evidence.

Final review: author self-review (no subagent tool). Scope-limited external
acceptance is pending; the uploaded original remains immutable.
